WEBVTT

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:45.950
What a nice wind.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:52.840
Yeah?

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.050
Be quiet.

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.630
Give me a break already.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:00.870
What exactly do you find so fascinating about me?

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:06.420
True, there isn't a single thing interesting about you.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:07.990
Frankly, you're pretty unpleasant.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.900
There's not a single thing interesting about you!

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:14.730
I heard you already.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:16.790
Why'd you say it twice?

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:19.450
Geez, I hate people like you.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:24.400
You sure about that?

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:27.330
What?  I do!

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:31.340
But wasn't it you who called out to me, first, Touma?

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:36.460
That's right.  And I've regretted it ever since.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:37.460
Get away from me!

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:50.920
Zoom!

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:53.590
Airplane!

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:00.820
Now then, we begin

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:06.030
Kazamatsuri Touma vs. Kageyama Torako

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:08.290
Kageyama Torako!

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.970
Kazamatsuri Touma!

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:15.710
The history of their battle!

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:19.970
Touma pisses me off, <i>soooo</i> much!

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.620
Touma?  Does she mean Kazamatsuri-san?

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.050
I think so.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.840
I wonder what happened?

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:28.390
Perhaps they had a fight again or-

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:30.130
Listen to me, Ayu!

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:32.680
She... She...

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:35.890
Touma!

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:40.820
Touma!  Touma!

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:42.980
Let me borrow your eraser!

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.510
Touma, hey!

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.240
Don't give me that!

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:00.380
Don't touch me!

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.720
...is what she said, to <i>me</i>!

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:06.150
She told me not to touch her!

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:07.550
You know?

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:09.430
I can understand those feelings.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:11.310
Whose feelings?

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.580
My feelings, right?

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:19.140
Despite the fact you've been trying your best right since you came to this school.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:23.800
That's right.  I've been putting my entire heart into bugging her, and yet...

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:32.230
She hasn't opened up to me even one bit!

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:33.240
Bugging her?

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:34.960
Isn't that why?

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:48.720
I like peace and quiet.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.710
That's why I like to be alone.

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:00.980
And yet, that damn idiot woman...

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.900
What's her purpose?

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.710
Damn, damn, damn, damn, damn, damn!

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:27.490
But, at least this place calms me down.

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:32.480
I'm glad I came to this school.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:39.460
The rules are lenient, they have a lot of facilities, and the library is big, that's what's important.

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:50.200
I wonder why I chose this school?

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:01.790
Noway! Noway! Noway! Noway!

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:06.910
It's just cause she's so persistent.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:10.510
This sucks!  I remembered something weird...

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:30.160
You're...

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:35.830
She's one of Kageyama Torako's underlings.  Saotome, was it?

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:41.290
What do you want?

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.210
You dropped your bookmark.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:51.050
T-Thanks.

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:07.870
Later.

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:17.660
What pretty eyes...

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:21.610
Weirdo...

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:24.890
Kageyama's surrounded by a bunch of weirdos.

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:27.880
Our class is filled with weirdos...

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:32.180
Like I care!

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.840
How should I make her my friend?

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:36.850
You don't give up, do you, Torako-san?

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:40.070
If I say I'm gonna do it, I'm gonna do it!

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:41.600
Until I'm victorious. there's nothing else I want!

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.850
I'll untwist that twisted personality!

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:47.800
Have you prepared any countermeasures, Private 3rd Class Nonomura?

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:48.980
Private 3rd class?

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:54.350
Um, Torako-san, about that...

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:59.200
Why are you so obsessed with Kazamatsuri-san, Torako-san?

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:03.250
I'm obsessed?

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:06.460
It looks that way to me, anyway...

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:10.310
Well, yeah, I'm obsessed.

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:14.170
Is that so?

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:15.920
Yeah, it is.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.350
Oh.

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:23.040
It's her.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:26.810
She's one of Kageyama's friends; the one that's like some kind of weird ojou-sama.

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:30.680
It seems like Torako-san's meddling has had an effect on her.

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:32.530
How pitiful.

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:34.940
Same as me.

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:41.200
Now, if you excuse me.  Fare thee well.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.550
"Fare thee well?"

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:48.170
I've never had that said to me since the day I was born.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:51.130
She's also a serious weirdo, I see.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:07.110
Just calm down.

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:11.030
This is my final frontier.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:12.150
Or something like that.

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:19.450
I'll read here.

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:44.120
You want something?

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:48.890
N-No... Nothing.

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:54.180
She's also one of Kageyama's cohorts.

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:55.440
Weirdo.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:00.280
Matsuri-san...

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:10.960
Kazamatsuri-san, do you hate Torako-san?

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:13.750
Why do you always use polite speech?

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:20.600
U-Um... a habit, I guess.

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:25.810
Don't talk to me using polite speech, okay?

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:26.820
Okay!

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:32.980
Um, that wasn't polite speech, I was just politely affirming.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:33.900
I hate her.

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:39.180
So this is your cellphone, Teach?

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:42.300
Kageyama, you've really been coming to the teacher's office a lot lately.

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:42.990
You think?

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:45.260
Are you worried about something?

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:46.750
Is this one of the ones that can transform?

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:48.220
Seems like it.

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:49.250
Nope.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:50.900
Stop playing around with it!

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:52.120
What are you doing?

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:55.490
But it won't move.

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:58.040
You're pushing it the wrong way!

00:10:58.040 --> 00:10:59.240
The wrong way?

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:01.170
The wrong way?

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:03.390
No, no!

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:04.480
Oh, like this!

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:06.590
Give it here!

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:07.770
It'll be fine.

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:10.160
W-Wait, don't force it!

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:15.610
Goddamn you!

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.120
That's the newest model!

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:19.210
Don't think you'll get away with just an apology!

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:20.250
Sorry!

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:21.430
I'll make it up to you!

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:23.120
Look at what you've done!

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:25.460
...like that.

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:26.700
She's an idiot!

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.120
Don't you realize she's an idiot?

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:29.640
The poor teacher...

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:31.580
Torako-san...

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:37.670
I hate empty-headed idiots you can't rely on who cause trouble for others!

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:46.470
However, it looks like Torako-san wants to be friends with you no matter what, Kazamatsuri-san...

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:47.850
Like I care!

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:54.770
I really like Torako-san.

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:59.980
I've always been really, really bad at making friends.

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:07.070
That's why I was so happy when Torako-san and I have got along together so well after we started here.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:19.470
Torako-san enjoys herself everyday, smiling, so I can...

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:20.460
Enough.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:22.950
It's embarrassing just listening to you.

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:26.550
S-S-Sorry!

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:31.140
Well, anyway, that's why I won't be friends with Kageyama.

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:33.140
I'm going back.

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:38.690
In that case, would you be my friend?

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:42.030
I'll think about it.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:44.530
Quit it with the polite speech though.

00:12:57.960 --> 00:12:59.790
What a nice wind!

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:02.000
Give me a break already.

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:04.510
What exactly do you find so fascinating about me?

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:08.180
True, there isn't a single thing interesting about you.

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:09.570
Frankly, you're pretty unpleasant.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.890
There's not a single thing interesting about you!

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:14.050
I heard you already.

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:15.850
Why'd you say it twice?

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:19.600
Geez, I hate people like you.

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:24.050
But wasn't it you who called out to me, first, Touma?

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:25.790
Too close.

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:28.160
That's right.  Get back!

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:32.360
And I've regretted it ever since.

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:43.550
This school's really big.

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:47.720
Where's everyone else?

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:51.430
Shoot, did I get separated from the group?

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:12.620
Drop something?

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:25.560
My hair band flew off.

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:29.850
Here, I'm not using this.

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:31.390
You sure?

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:33.350
Thanks.

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:38.020
Are you visiting the school too?

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:39.350
Yeah.

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:40.810
Me too!

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:44.490
Isn't it just insanely big?

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:47.260
It's because it also has a elementary and middle school.

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:48.860
Oh?

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:50.590
That's what it says in the pamphlet.

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:52.660
I didn't bother reading it.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:53.410
Read it.

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:57.240
I came to check it out cause my family said to go here.

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:02.930
But this place might be pretty good!

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:08.080
The wind feels really nice... Maybe because it's on a high spot?

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:11.200
Guess I should try getting in here.

00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:13.470
How about you?

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:17.800
I've already applied.

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:26.610
Then, if we end up getting in, let's be friends!

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:31.560
I-I'll think about it.

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:40.430
What are you doing here?

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:44.520
I shall tell you even had you not asked, Chief of Staff Kazamatsuri!

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:46.800
Chief of Staff?  What is with that?

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:48.840
I'm a private 3rd class.

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:50.840
So you really want to know, eh?

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:53.420
Just spill it already, you're killin' me here!

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:58.310
We simply came here to partake of our lunches atop the roof, my friend.

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:01.850
Really?  Then would you eat on that bench over there?

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:05.190
Like hell I will!

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:06.260
I knew it!

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:07.550
What a nice view!

00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:08.820
Wow!

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:12.260
I have attended here since elementary school, but this is the first time I have been on the roof.

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:14.610
It feels really nice.

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:18.630
Touma, look here.  Ayu's gonna give ya your lunch.

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:19.300
Huh?

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:21.030
A little bit of happiness!

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:22.160
Huh?

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:25.370
You always just have bread, don't you, Matsuri-chan?

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:27.080
So, here.

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:28.090
Huh?

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.950
Don't be so shocked.

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:32.870
Matsuri-chan?  You mean me?

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:34.050
That's what you're surprised at?

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:36.510
Yeah.

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:39.850
Kaza...matsuri-chan.

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:43.090
Get it, Matsuri-chan?

00:16:43.090 --> 00:16:44.430
What are you doing?

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:47.730
I made plenty of dishes for you.

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:50.260
Say "Ah!"

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:51.070
Torako-san!

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:55.300
What's with her?

00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:56.540
Hey, Suzu!

00:16:56.540 --> 00:16:58.030
Was this really for me?

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:01.850
Wait, Ayu, you made this yourself?

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:02.360
Yeah.

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:03.750
I love to cook!

00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:05.540
You're the perfect woman.

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:07.630
Too cramped...

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:09.460
This is good.

00:17:15.650 --> 00:17:17.030
Hey, Hitsugi.

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:17.810
What?

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:20.630
Why do we eat lunch together?

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:24.930
Because we're friends?

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:28.280
Eating together...

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:31.990
Adults do such a thing to evaluate their own communication.

00:17:31.990 --> 00:17:35.380
Commu... Communication?

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:39.280
The lubrication of human interpersonal relationships.

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:41.070
Lubrication?

00:17:41.070 --> 00:17:41.990
What?

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:46.320
Even if we didn't, friends are friends, right?

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:49.580
But, it tastes better when we're together.

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:52.400
There is no scientific basis for that.

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:56.810
Just kidding!

00:17:56.810 --> 00:18:00.510
Of course food tastes better when eating with your friends!

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:08.560
I ended up eating with them!

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:09.880
I'm being swept along...

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:11.480
You got rice stuck on your cheeky.

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:16.570
Isn't that nice, Kageyama-kun?

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:19.880
All right!

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:22.020
We're gonna do it too!

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:24.080
Do what?

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:27.600
Deepen our friendship!

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:28.590
Yuck.

00:18:28.590 --> 00:18:30.360
What are you talking about?

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:33.070
There's only one reason that I could have asked you here today.

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:34.940
Spit it out already.

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:36.320
Wait just a moment now.

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:39.560
You also need time to prepare yourselves emotionally, I suppose.

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:45.920
My sweet proposal has left your glass hearts all aflutter, asparkle, alighted!

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:47.520
Show of hands:  Who's leaving?

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:48.950
Wait!

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:50.610
Give it up!

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:55.070
I was just thinking we should all eat lunch together!

00:18:56.270 --> 00:18:58.700
Fine with me.

00:18:58.700 --> 00:18:59.950
I like the idea.

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:02.050
What a pain.

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:07.780
More specifically, I'm hankhankhankering for one of Ayu-tan's homemade lunches!

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:11.490
Hankhankhankering?

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:13.210
It means she really wants to eat one.

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:16.390
So, how are everyone's lunches?

00:19:16.390 --> 00:19:17.400
Let's have a look!

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:19.710
Hurry, no need to be embarrassed.

00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:20.550
I'll be good.

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:22.720
Kobayashi Koma

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:22.720
Convenience Store Bento

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:23.840
Makunouchi Ushio

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:23.840
Convenience Store Bread

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:23.840
Jam-Butter Bread

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:23.840
Kouign Amann (Butter Cake)

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:26.930
Suzugasaki Chie

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:26.930
Five Nikuman (Meat Bun)

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:30.230
I would've figured Kobayashi-kun for a boxed lunch, yes...

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:32.770
I guess I wasn't really expecting anything else.

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:37.650
But I at least thought there would be something better for lunch.

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:40.190
Glasses girl, what the heck is with you?!

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:42.650
Sorry, today I...

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:45.110
Five meat buns?

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:48.530
I was thinking I could eat them while doing some work.

00:19:48.530 --> 00:19:49.970
Eating while working?

00:19:49.970 --> 00:19:51.670
That is not the womanly thing to do.

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:54.980
Well, I guess it's not out of character for her.

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:57.010
But this is all just out of whack.

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:59.880
Think a little bit about your health.

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:03.510
Oba-kun!

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:04.500
What?

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:07.430
All you have is snack food!

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:09.520
Yup, all snack food!

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:11.820
You should have a balanced diet!

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:13.990
I have lots of different kinds.

00:20:13.990 --> 00:20:16.950
I have potato flavor, corn flavor, chicken flavor...

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:21.610
Different flavored chips or soda doesn't count, geez!

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:24.790
And snack food isn't for meals in the first place!

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:28.490
How lamentable!

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:31.230
And you call yourselves women.

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:34.000
Yes, Tsubomiya-kun?

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:35.320
You...

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:40.340
Mine is homemade.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:42.310
My mother made it.

00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:43.940
Homemade?

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:47.270
Then, you already ate it?

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:48.430
No.

00:20:49.690 --> 00:20:51.890
I haven't eaten it.

00:20:52.630 --> 00:20:55.810
Right about now, my lunch is...

00:20:58.090 --> 00:21:00.520
What's with her reaction?

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:06.600
Amagasa-sensei, you have a box lunch today?

00:21:06.600 --> 00:21:07.730
That's rare.

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:12.310
Well, there was some stuff and things and...

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:13.620
This is how it turned out.

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:18.420
How was it?

00:21:22.330 --> 00:21:24.320
So we're even now, 'kay?

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:28.880
Not gonna say thanks?

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:36.020
Thanks...

00:21:43.980 --> 00:21:45.030
Thank you!

00:23:21.620 --> 00:23:22.990
What's on Hyakko<i> next week?</i>

00:23:22.990 --> 00:23:24.120
"Escape from the Tiger's Jaw"

00:23:24.120 --> 00:23:25.590
It's about dodgeball, then?

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:27.900
It's a giant free-for-all with the entire cast thrown in!

00:23:27.900 --> 00:23:29.510
Totally different feeling than today, huh?

00:23:29.780 --> 00:23:32.470
That's what makes this show so great!

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:33.790
Tune in next time!
